<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation Barbarossa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation Barbarossa was the German invasion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, launched on 22 June 1941 by some three million German troops with Romanian, Finnish and other allied forces. It destroyed much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> in huge encirclements at Białystok–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minsk">Minsk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> and reached the outskirts of Leningrad and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, but the Soviet counter-offensive before Moscow in December 1941 ended Hitler's hope of a quick victory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-barbarossa.jpg" alt="Operation Barbarossa" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bundesarchiv, Bild 146-1974-099-19 / Kempe / CC-BY-SA 3.0; Samaryi Guraryi / Самарий Гурарий; Ustinov / Александр Устинов … · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Operation_Barbarossa_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
